              {
                "text": "**Analyzing Visual Input**\n\nI'm focusing on the visual data. My current focus is dissecting Example 1. It seems like the training examples are built from colored rectangular frames that enclose colored dots/pixels. I have identified a red box with a height of 6 and width of 5. Next, I will look at the location of the pixels.\n\n\n**Interpreting Pixel Relationships**\n\nI'm now diving into Example 2. I've broken down the boxes: magenta (6), teal (8), and blue (1). I am examining the pixel distribution within each box, and tallying the counts. Magenta has four non-zero pixels. Teal has none. Blue has a single pixel. It's becoming clearer that the output is constructed by a count of pixels inside each box, ordered by the left-most box. My updated interpretation is that it is a left-to-right processing of boxes, counting how many non-zero pixels are inside the box, and that number defines how many times the number of the box appears!\n\n\n",
